This directory is managed by Flask-Migrate and Alembic.

Create a migration after adding or changing SQLAlchemy models:

    flask --app backend/run.py db migrate -m "describe the schema change"

Review the generated migration carefully before applying it:

    flask --app backend/run.py db upgrade

Never edit an already-applied migration to change production schema history. Add a new migration instead.

## Initial multi-company schema

The first migration creates global users, companies, and company memberships. It is
applied in CI against PostgreSQL 16 before the test suite runs.

The migration is additive and has a downgrade that drops only these three new
tables. Before applying future production migrations, take a database backup and
review the generated SQL. This initial schema does not yet enable PostgreSQL row
level security or authenticate users; those controls require the later
company-context and authentication milestones.
